> possible so you can install on a brand new GS320 just like an old
> AS200 4/233.

BWX is not a kind of CPU instruction set extension for optimization
(like MMX on pentiums) it provides a way to do i/o by mapping the 
device's register into memory in a (relatively) simple way.

On non-BWX capaple machines, emulating the i386 inb/outb operators is 
more
complicated and support for that is not present in OpenBSD.

So this is not just a matter of re-compilation.

Matthieu Herrb

